## Summary
This article critiques the racist notion that elite institutions routinely hire less qualified Black faculty, challenging the myth of Black intellectual inferiority. It addresses racial bias in academic hiring practices and advocates for equal recognition of Black faculty's qualifications.

## Key Points
- The article denounces the racist idea that Black faculty hired at elite institutions are not fully qualified.
- It rejects the myth of Black intellectual inferiority in academic contexts.
- It highlights institutional racism and equity issues in higher education hiring.
- It emphasizes the need to recognize the full intellectual capabilities of Black faculty.


